[967.236464, "o", "[Profiling] Using device: cuda:0 NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3, warm up 3, trials 30\r\ncoop G=8 nt=512: mean 0.9396 min 0.9362 ok=True\r\n[Profiling] Using device: cuda:0 NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3, warm up 3, trials 30\r\ncoop G=8 nt=1024: mean 0.5450 min 0.5409 ok=True\r\n[Profiling] Using device: cuda:0 NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3, warm up 3, trials 30\r\ncoop G=16 nt=512: mean 0.5440 min 0.5406 ok=True\r\ncoop G=16 nt=1024: FAIL AcceleratorError CUDA error: too many blocks in cooperative launch\r\nSearch for `cudaErrorCooperativeLaunchTooLarge' in https://docs.nvidia.com/cuda/cuda-runtime-api/group__CUDART__TYPES.html for more information.\r\nCUDA kernel errors might be asynchronously reported at some other API call, so the stacktrace below might be incorrect.\r\nFor debugging consider passing CUDA_LAUNCH_BLOCKING=1\r\nCompile with `TORCH_USE_CUDA_DSA` to enable device-side assertions.\r\n\r\n"]
